Apple makes several other products that it categorizes as "Wearables, Home and Accessories".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Leswing |first=Kif |date=January 28, 2020 |title=Apple's fastest-growing business segment, which includes AirPods and Watch, is now bigger than Mac |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2020/01/28/apple-wearables-home-and-accessories-segment-now-bigger-than-mac.html |access-date=October 19, 2022 |website=CNBC |language=en |archive-date=October 19, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221019225049/https://www.cnbc.com/2020/01/28/apple-wearables-home-and-accessories-segment-now-bigger-than-mac.html |url-status=live}}</ref> These products include the [[Apple headphones|AirPods]] line of wireless headphones, [[Apple TV (device)|Apple TV]] digital media players, [[Apple Watch]] smartwatches, [[Beats Electronics|Beats]] headphones, [[HomePod]] smart speakers, and the [[Vision Pro]] mixed reality headset. {{As of|2025|pre=the end of}}, this broad line of products comprises about nine percent of the company's revenues.<ref name="Apple-10-K-Report-2025" />

=== Services ===
Apple also generates revenue from a range of services, including commissions from the [[App Store (Apple)|App Store]] on app sales and in-app purchases, extended warranties through [[AppleCare+]], cloud storage through [[iCloud+]], and payment services through the [[Apple Card]] credit card and [[Apple Pay]] platform. The company also provides digital content services, including [[Apple Books]], [[Apple Fitness+]], [[Apple Music]], [[Apple News]], [[Apple TV (streaming service)|Apple TV]], and the [[iTunes Store]]. [[Apple One]] bundles several of these services into a single subscription. Since 2019, Apple has placed greater emphasis on expanding its services business as a source of recurring revenue.<ref name="AppleVideoRevenue2">{{Cite news |last=Pullen |first=John Patrick |date=March 24, 2019 |title=Apple's Two-Word Plan for the Future of the Internet: Subscribe Now |url=http://fortune.com/2019/03/24/watch-apple-event-live-stream-television-news-service |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190325135825/http://fortune.com/2019/03/24/watch-apple-event-live-stream-television-news-service |archive-date=March 25, 2019 |access-date=March 25, 2019 |work=[[Forbes]]}}</ref> {{As of|2025|pre=the end of}}, services comprise about 26% of the company's revenue.<ref name="Apple-10-K-Report-2025" />
